2	// projects, and what's in each - read afresh from the projects every time,
3	// since a turn, a build or a push may have changed any of them.
4	//
5	// The model is the shape of the design's states: times are prepared strings
6	// ("4 minutes ago"), and needs are kept in the order they arrived, oldest
7	// first, for the view to show newest first.
8	//
9	// How a design stands, read for its In progress line:
10	//   question      the newest session's last turn ended asking something (its
11	//                 last words end with "?"); until they answer
12	//   finished      a turn ended; until they open its session, or for a week (R-8hc)
13	//   stopped       a build under way on a branch, with no turn running
14	//   to-build      approved pages the app doesn't have yet
15	//   pull-request  a branch pushed for review; until it's merged
16	// Of these, only what the person must act on needs them (R-n4v): a question,
17	// a stopped build and a turn that ended with an error. The rest the page
18	// already says where each design is listed.
19	// A design the agent is working on needs nothing yet: that's in the bar.
